<!--
  NEGATIVE FIXTURE. Do not "fix" the missing BToA0Tag below.

  Clause 8.10.3 c) says "Whenever an AToBxTag is present, its paired BToAxTag
  shall also be present", and 8.10.6 repeats it for the Display case. This
  profile has an AToB0Tag and no BToA0Tag.

  The general validator does not catch this. The Display branch of
  CIccProfile::CheckRequiredTags() tests AToB0 and BToA0 only as a pair against
  the matrix/TRC alternative: if either is absent it falls back to requiring the
  matrix column and TRC tags, so a profile carrying A2B0, no B2A0, and a
  complete matrix/TRC set satisfies it without comment. The HDR rule is what
  makes the unpaired tag visible.

  Expected: iccFromXml saves the profile, and iccDumpProfile -v reports
    "HDR: AToB0Tag present without its paired BToA0Tag"
  See Testing/expected-invalid-fromxml.tsv.
-->
